    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "July 8th, 2006, item number 155. Today's special guest is Senator Ted Stevens from Alaska. Before we get into our interview with Senator Stevens, a couple quick news and notes. First off, as always, if you have any feedback you'd like to share with the audience, give us a call at 206-666-4357. That's 206-666-HELP. You can also send audio feedback to podcast411 at gmail.com. And our latest way to get us feedback is with the My Chingo service, which you can find on Podcast411.com, upper left-hand side, click on the My Chingo button and you can record directly from your computer. While I was at NOMEDEX, I was interviewed by the lip gloss and laptops podcast and that interview is now available on their show. So if you'd like to hear me on the other side of the mic talking a little bit about NOMEDEX, go over to their podcast, check it out. Link will be in the show notes as always. The second item on the news and notes is I have to give you a warning. You need to look out for link spammers. There is one site now that is aggressively looking for cross links. Don't do it. Don't help out these spammers. One right now when you go to their site The site's nothing more than a complete sham. There's no real information. They claim to be this podcast information site, but it's nothing more than a link spam with ad words, and they're just trying to make money off us and off the name podcasting. Matter of fact, you'll know it's their site because they spell podcast, P-O-D, space, C-A-S-T. Yep, they do it as two different words. So that tells you as much as you need to know about this company. If you want to know their exact URL and you're afraid you may have linked to them by mistake, Shoot me an email, I'll tell you offline, but I'm not gonna give many PR on the show. Again, just watch out for the link spammers. Now I have some feedback here to play that came in through the My Chingo service. Here we go.",
