  {
    "episode_id": 49762,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49762.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Hi Rob, this is Jamie Davis, the Pod Medic from the MedicCast Podcast. I just wanted to give you a couple of quick comments. First of all, thanks for finding my Chingo audio recorder. This is excellent. I've already added it to the MedicCast site and I'm looking forward to having this great way for getting audio comments directly from my listeners. The other thing is I just finished your book. tricks of the podcasting masters and my primary comment is that you're right on the money with saying that people need to be passionate about the topics they podcast. And I think that's why I got into what I do. My Metacast is a podcast for EMTs and paramedics just like me and a source for informational news and continuing education ideas and just a way for me to bounce ideas that are rattling around my brain out there for other people just like me. And I think that's really what podcasting is all about. The other thing that your book pointed out for me was that I was headed in the right direction. As I read about marketing and about getting information out there about my podcast, it let me know that I was thinking about doing the right things and also gave me some great ideas to expand on what I was already thinking about. So excellent book, I highly recommend it, and I just want to let both you and her know that it was just an excellent job. Thanks a lot. Keep up the good work. I look forward to a lot of great podcast interviews from you in the future. The information you provide on your site and through your podcast are invaluable tools for everybody out there that's podcasting. Thanks a lot. This is Jamie Davis, the Pod Medic from the MedicCast Podcast saying, thanks a lot for all your help.",
